From 830cdd094df3b12c75c2ebd14467b1744f1ce024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 14:07:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): per-harness agent-agnostic dispatch delivery
 (W1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Make W1 auto-trigger truly agent-agnostic by delivering the using-forge dispatch
bootstrap on each harness's native always-on surface, by SURFACE TYPE (never
harness-name branching).

- Fix the FALSE capability matrix: hook-renderer SESSION_START_SUPPORT claimed
  Cursor has "no-session-start-surface" (wrong — Cursor auto-applies rules every
  session). Reasons are now honest and name the delivery surface: cursor
  delivered-via-rule-surface, codex delivered-via-agents-md, hermes
  delivered-via-cli-fallback. New BOOTSTRAP_DELIVERY data table (claude=hook,
  cursor=rule, codex=agents-md, hermes=cli-fallback). Refresh S15/S7 matrix docs.
- AGENTS.md generator (agents-config.generateAgentsMdContent): add a thin "Skill
  Dispatch" pointer to using-forge + `forge skill for` — the always-on carrier for
  Codex (native AGENTS.md), Claude (CLAUDE.md @AGENTS.md), Hermes (forge orient).
  Satisfies follow-up f954b2b9 via the sanctioned generator path (no protected
  AGENTS.md hand-edit). Full 1%-rule stays only in the skill (no duplication).
- Cursor rule surface: NEW canonical rules/using-forge.md (alwaysApply:true thin
  pointer) + CURSOR_RULE_FILES entry → renders .cursor/rules/using-forge.mdc.
- Parity test (mechanism, not identity): iterates delivery SURFACES, asserts the
  dispatch pointer on each; loops HARNESS_IDS asserting every rendered:false
  harness has a real bootstrap surface or the explicit cli-fallback marker; drift
  assertion added to the rules gate so the fanned-out copies can't lose the pointer.

Deferred to epic 90f2f631 (noted): rendering the actual Cursor .cursor/hooks.json
sessionStart / Codex [hooks] SessionStart — rule + AGENTS.md carriers suffice now
and avoid triple-inject.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
